  "narrative": "QuarterRig utilizes the HTTPS protocol for C2 communication, which is encrypted using RC4 encryption. The payload of the BMP file is capable of requesting the malware to read or write files, inject shellcode into remote processes, or run commands via cmd.exe. Both samples share similarities in their utilization of dynamically resolved syscalls, employing online storage providers like [REDACTED_MALWARE] for C2 communications, and camouflaging C2 communications as benign files \u0000MP3 in the earlier analysis and BMP in the more recent samples).",
